===========================================================================
Title: GOBASIC v5.0 for desktop
Developer: Luyao Zou
Date: Feb 2017
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Feature Updated:
>> Improve partition function interpolation for internal rotation.
   The Q(T)=a*T^b form used in v4.5 is not sufficient to account for
   the contribution from internal rotation and torsion motions.
   Update the functional form to
   Q(T) = a(1) * T^a(2) * (a(3) + exp(a(4)/T))

>> Remove Q(T) fitting routine. Each molecule needs its own treatment
   based on its top, internal rotation, vibrational states, and what goes into
   the catalog.

>> Fit Q(T) externally, save the coefficients to *par.co files, and
   load them into GOBASIC via the 'parco' cell array.

>> Update Code Files:
   definevars.m     -- add parco cell array.
   analysisscript.m -- load parco coefficients.
   tausim.m         -- update partition function interpolation.
   writeresult.m    -- update version tag. Output par coefficients in Table.txt
   comp_label_gen.py -- update label generator.
   partfunc.m       -- disable (ignore) this file.

===========================================================================
Title: GOBASIC v4.5 for desktop
Developer: Luyao Zou
Date: Dec 2015
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Feature Updated:
>> Improve partition function extrapolation.
   Previous versions used Q(T) = a*T^{3/2}, where a is fitted.
   This function form is only valid when molecule is nonlinear and has no
   internal rotation or tunneling levels.
   Current version implements Q(T) = a*T^b where both a and b are fitted.

>> Fix a bug in displayresult.m, where the log10 values of column density
   was displayed.

>> Move 'range' from analysisscript.m to definevars.m for easier configuration.
   The value of 'range' should be set once for all and held unvaried for a
   particular line survey data. Otherwise previous fit import will raise
   array dimension error.
   However, for different set of line surveys, especially those at different
   frequency bands, the value of 'range' should be adjusted accordingly to
   cover the full Gaussian profile. See more details in GOBASICAlgorithm.pdf

>> Update Code Files:
   definevars.m     -- move 'range' here
   analysisscript.m -- remove 'range'. Update 'aco' to reflect change in
                       partition function calculation.
   partfunc.m       -- update partition function extrapolation procedure.
                       outputs array (a,b) instead of number a
   tausim.m         -- reflect the change of 'aco' from number to cell array
   totalsim.m       -- reflect the change of 'aco' from number to cell array
   err.m            -- reflect the change of 'aco' from number to cell array
   displayresult.m  -- Fix the bug of displaying log10 column density
   writeresult.m    -- update version tag


===========================================================================
Title: GOBASIC v4.4 for desktop
Developer: Luyao Zou
Date: June 2015
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Feature Updated:
>> Rescale temperature input by dividing 100 (rescale 1000 to 10)
   instead of taking natural logarithm. This is because a linear rescaling
   allows negative temperature input, which can be used to fit masers.

>> Update uncertainty estimation. Calculate full variance-covariance
   matrix, instead of stand-alone ones for each component.

>> Update output file format. Constraint the length of lines in
   FitTable.txt below 80 characters for easier reading.

>> Move beamdilution calculation & previous fit importation into
   analysisscript.m so that they can be called and calculated once for all.

>> Updated Code Files:
   tausim.m  -- update equations for tau
   totalsim.m  -- update equations for totalsim
   analysisscript.m  -- refactored, include beamdilution calc & previous
                        fit import
   anonfun4.m -- update equations for creating fitting function
   definevars.m  -- transpose init, low and up matrices to put the
                    parameters for each component in the same column
   err.m      -- update uncertainty estimation to match the new spectral
                 generating function
   linecenter.m  -- transpose row/column to match the new matrix orientation
   optest.m   -- update output and uncertainty handling section to match
                 the new spectral generating function
   displayresult.m -- update to match the change of fitted parameter matrix
   writeresult.m   -- update output table format
   analysisscript.m -- update previous fit importation


===========================================================================
Title: GOBASIC v4.3 for desktop
Developer: Luyao Zou
Date: Feb 2015
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Feature Updated:
>> The gaussian profile we use in GOBASIC is incorrect, as pointed out by
   an anonymous referee. The gaussian function should be performed on the
   optical depth \tau, thus goes into the exponential exp(-\tau), instead
   of directly multiplied to the brightness temperature evaluated at the
   peak center of a transition.

>> The beam size is calculated on the fly due to its dependence on the
   wavelength. The diameter of the telescope, instead of the source size,
   is taken as an user input. Then at each transition frequency, a beam
   size is generated using
   \theta_b = 1.39*wavelength/(D*pi)*180*3600 (arcsec)
   where wavelength is converted from the center frequency of the given
   molecular transition, and D is the dish diameter

>> Fixed an subtle mistake in err.m

>> Updated Code files:
   definevars.m   --  update input parameter
   analysisscript.m -- remove calculation of a universal beam filling factor
   anonfun4.m     --  update function arguments
   err.m          --  update uncertainty calculation
   linecalc.m     --  update unit conversion of Agu
   optest.m       --  update uncertainty calculation
   totalsim.m     --  update equations and arguments
   writeresult.m  --  update version tag


>> Deleted Code files:
   molsim.m
   maxtemp.m
   [no longer needed. Functions combined in 'totalsim.m']


