Title: GOBASIC v4.2 for desktop
Developer: Luyao Zou
Date: Dec 2014
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Feature Updated:
>> Add a cut-off option of upper state energy for the transitions. Now the
   user can also knock-off undesired warm lines or cold lines before the
   fit.

>> Modify the way of spectra synthesis in 'molsim.m'
   The x-data window opened for generating Gaussian line-profiles are
   centered around shifted line centers, instead of line centers from the
   catalog. This modification is able to prevent missing spectra at large
   shift parameters.
   See 'GOBASIC_Algorithm.pdf' for detailed code information

>> Added Code file:
   linecenter.m  -- replace jlabel_gen.m

>> Deleted Code files:
   jlabel_gen.m


===========================================================================
Title: GOBASIC v4.1 for desktop
Developer: Luyao Zou
Date: Sept 2014
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Feature Updated:
>> Add a python script, 'comp_label_gen.py' to automatically generate the
   code with the correct Matlab format for GOBASIC 'definevars.m' catalog
   section. It also generates the corresponding label of the fitting
   components for GOBASIC output files, so that one do not need to write
   down the names and order of 20+ components for each fitting job.

   The user need to create a text file of the component name list. Each
   name takes a single line. If one needs to fit multiple velocity
   components for a given molecule, the catalog and partition function
   file names need to be duplicated in the list. The python script will
   output a file called 'component_label.m' with the correct Matlab
   format, and the user can copy that to the corresponding section in
   'definevars.m'


>> Add labels to the legend, and '*Fit.csv' files for each column. The
   labels are typeset in 'definevars.m' manually, and the user may take
   the advantage of the python script. If the labels are left blank,
   by default fit+number 'fit#' will be used as component labels.

>> The user may need to customize the script for their catalog directory
   and naming system. Currently, the output format of 'comp_label_gen.py'
   is '../CatalogFile/MoleculeName.txt' for catalog files
      '../CatalogFile/MoleculeNamepar.par' for partition function files,
   and 'MoleculeName' for labels.

>> v4.1 is compatible with v4.0 on importing and exporting data. The only
   difference is that v4.1 is capable of adding customized labels to better
   mark all the components fitted


